phoneme_description.9:
We have seen the intonation accents; we shall now see the pronunciation accents, which are:
The circumflex accent (^);
The breve accent (v);
The beard (') which affects u and o so as to change their value entirely.
It is evident that the intonation accent does not exclude the pronunciation accent and that a vowel can possess them simultaneously, as we shall see from the examples that follow.
